Z||000000||DreXteR||09-23-2001||06:51 PM||||Hi, Does it worth? I will be running high performance engine in there. <P>Im consudering the change, what are the pros and cons? Gain and loose? <P>Thanx<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/halfpole.gif">        <BR>  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||09-23-2001||07:14 PM||||I've got the 4.10 four speed in mine. If I ever have to do anything with the trans, I am putting an Isuzu 5 speed back in there. I like the 4 speed's strength and gearing, but eventually I want to make some lengthy road trips and the 4 speed kind of stinks at 75 MPH.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||09-23-2001||07:58 PM||||I dont know the ratio of my tranny. Certenly most of the time Im @ the highway. <P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000003||DreXteR||09-24-2001||12:10 AM||||.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||09-24-2001||12:39 AM||||The 4:10 four speed is great for quick acceleration but was geared for the 55mph speed limits.  I have that 4 speed in my '84 SE and although everything is smooth sailing at 70-75mph, the tach is at 3,500rpm.<P>I like having the 4:10 gears with the 2.5L, but I catch myself every once in a while looking to grab another gear but can't.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||09-24-2001||12:58 AM||||I have a 4:10 gear in my 3.4 till it cracked. Don't know if the tranny was bad or it I ran it to hard a few times that made it break.  The 4:10 on the highway is not all that bad.  I actually loved my 4-speed till it died on me.  The acceleration was awsome with it.  If I were you I would try to test drive eachone before choosing.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DreXteR||09-24-2001||01:07 AM||||How I can determine the ratio of my tranny?<P>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ferrari_cdn||09-24-2001||03:36 AM||||I have the 4spd too.  You said you might have drove it hard and cracked it, you mean by revving it high?  I sometimes shifted to second when I was at 3000 or 4000, is that too high?  When I'm cruising the city roads @60 kph (40 mph maybe?)  I'm usually in third @3000.  Should I have that at fourth @2000?  I wasn't sure which is best, sometimes I slowed down to 40 kph and the engine ends up being in 1500 is Im still in fourth and it was sluggish when I try to accelerate.  Is that bad for the engine, trying to work hard against the clutch?  I was told I should keep the rpms down, but what is reasonable?  Shift down and when it reaches 2500 or 3000 then shift to the next gear?<P>When I try to make a left turn through an intersection, I sometimes do it fast and end up shifting @4000 to 4500, is that bad or okay only if I do it occasionally?  Here or there I pressed the clutch but released the gas at the same time so sometimes the rpms jumps to 5000.  (oops).<P>I'm not an expert in trannies yet.  I'm just starting at it (a week ago).  I wanted to hear advices or warnings because I don't want to shorten my engine's life.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG">  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||5
Z||000008||Leper||09-24-2001||04:08 AM||||Here's a list of Fiero transaxle ratios. <A HREF="http://www.gigaparts.com/users/fiero/gears.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gigaparts.com/users/fiero/gears.htm</A> <BR>If you have a v6 and a stock 4 speed, it's got a 3.65 final drive ratio. Mine revs about 3k at 80mph (I think)<P>The 84's had 2 different 4 speeds. The performance 4.10 geared trans and the economy 3.32 geared trans. the 4.10 had a .81 overdrive while the 3.32 had a .71 overdrive which seperated the highway speeds even more.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DreXteR||09-24-2001||02:39 PM||||.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||09-24-2001||03:54 PM||||Tire sizes play a part too.  <P>I love my 86 4 speed.  But I like it even more with my 225/45/17s  24.9" dia.  1st gear really gets you moving, but not far with small dia. tires.  On the highway...the engine is within its powerband(low side) and has plenty power to move out without downshifting.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Joe Torma||09-24-2001||03:54 PM||||Tire sizes play a part too.  <P>I love my 86 4 speed.  But I like it even more with my 225/45/17s  24.9" dia.  1st gear really gets you moving, but not far with small dia. tires.  On the highway...the engine is within its powerband(low side) and has plenty power to move out without downshifting.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
