Z||000017||terryk||09-27-2001||12:41 PM||||Were the 4.10's even available on the V6? I didn't think they were.<P>I've been pondering this swap too. I have a 4spd V6 and this Getrag sitting here. It's been rebuilt but I'm trying to decide if it's worth the swap. When I drive other 5 spd's, there are more gears, but I can't say they pull any better.<P>I have an excel spreadsheet that compares all of the trans. I guess I could upload it.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Formula||09-27-2001||12:44 PM||||I would put a 4 spd in mine if I go with a standard.  4 spd with 4.10s!<P>It gets driven at most once a week in the summer though so that may be different then your fieros.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigs.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||rogergarrison||09-27-2001||12:48 PM||||id say the 5 speed is really only better for long cruising gas milage, lower rpms on engine. I have 4 spd, and its fine for me as a standard. I think I just may have found a nice 87 V6 auto, curious to see how it compares. I needed the auto for in town driving mostly for a new project. I havent seen it yet, dont know what options it has but its only 38K for $700.||||reg||1
Z||000020||DreXteR||09-27-2001||02:21 PM||||I look over the trannies specs and the 4.10 dont come with v6 as standard equipment. If you have one should be a swap. Also the dif between the perf 4.10 from 84 and mine GT 86 are the final ratio, the gears are the same exept from 1st gear. The 5 speed is dif, all the gears are more strong plus adding another gear for economy or highway speed. Also the final ratio is smaller the the 4 speed v6.  Between my 4 speed and the 5speed the data sheet cleary say that the 5 speed would accelerate more and give me a better top end, plus fuel economy. How can the 4 speed accelerate faster??????  The only additional factor is the final ratio, my 4 speed have a bigger one. The 4.10 tranny have to be out of this evaluation because inst the one I have.<P>Please leave me some imput....    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>Thanx<P>DreX<p>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||MooCow||09-27-2001||03:58 PM||||I have the 4:10 tranny in my Fiero and it is faster off the line than any other 5-speed I have been in.  I love this tranny because of the gearing. Gas mileiage isnt to bad either. I get about 23 miles to the gallon city driving.  Only bad thing I can think of is you can't go faster than 110 MPH or you hit redline.  For me I don't like going that fast so it doesnt bother me.  I like stop like to stop like and 0-60's anything else I could care less about. Have mopre to say about this topic but I am in colege right now so when I get home I'll post more.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000022||I wish I had a GT||09-28-2001||10:58 AM||||How about the 4:10 tranny with a 3.8 engine?  am I pusing my luck?   I want acceleration and 1/4 time<P>------------------<BR>**I wish I had a GT**||||reg||1
Z||000023||LarryB||09-28-2001||02:47 PM||||Generally a bit easier to deal with the 4 speed because you don't need to shift *quite* as often, and you get a bit more out of it when running through the first 2 gears hard.<BR>I can also do a cleaner high-speed pass with the 4 speed without having to downshift. At 75MPH in 4th you're about 400RPM higher than a 5 speed in 5th.<P>The Getrag is a bit cleaner shifting overall especially when shifting into reverse but isn't anywhere as much an improvement over the Muncie is the Isuzu is.  <P>The only real knock I have against the 4 speed is that there feels like a bit of a dead spot between 2nd and 3rd because of the gearing.  1st -&gt; 2nd and 3rd -&gt; 4th are pretty good.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DreXteR:<BR><B>Why Larry???</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||DreXteR||09-28-2001||03:56 PM||||One clear factor is the reving time. The reving time in the 4 speed i beleive will be more tha the 5 speed. Thats a big concern to me because I will run a turbo setup, the fast the car revs the fast the turbo will spool, the sooner the turbo spool the power came early and no lag.<P>DreX<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Cooter||09-28-2001||07:46 PM||||Acceleration with the 4.10's and a stock (internally) 3.4? The G-Tech quarter mile says 14.55 has been the best and 14.88 on a pretty regular basis. This is shifting at 5200 rpms after a 1500 rpm launch.||||reg||1
Z||000026||DreXteR||09-28-2001||09:13 PM||||OK Nice but I DONT HAVE THE 4.10 tranny.<P>DreX||||reg||4
